Hi

On 02-05-2025 08:27, Charles Plessy wrote:
> Am I right that first I need to upload packages updated with adjusted
> build-dependencies, because otherwise the buildds will just rebuild the
> packages that were just removed?

With "adjusted build-dependencies" do you mean the Architecture field, 
or do you mean the "B-D-that-doesnt-exist [<arch-to-not-build>]" trick, 
or something else? Nowadays it's recommended to not handle this via the 
Architecture field but via that non-existing B-D [1]

You only need to do this at the bottom of the stack; everything that 
misses its build depends on an arch is not build. But yes, the 
ftp-master might need to remove things is one go and/or in the right 
order to prevent rebuilds.

Paul

[1] 
https://salsa.debian.org/debian/developers-reference/-/merge_requests/60/diffs

